    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (73.06) and **Kyle Schwarber** (65.53) headlining the lineup as the clear power anchors. Despite facing challenging arms in Luis Castillo and Suarez respectively, both possess elite xwOBA metrics that render them near-must starts, with **Schwarber** benefiting further from favorable park factors. **Trea Turner** (64.53) remains our most critical asset for the SB category; while he faces a decent arm in Suarez, his elite speed profile and top-of-the-order positioning outweigh the slight penalty for facing a tough lefty. We are also projecting significant contributions from **Carson Benge** (59.15), whose matchup against Montero provides the best SP-xERA delta of the day, allowing his upside to flourish in the leadoff spot.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Dillon Dingler**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 33.06 efficiency score. While he has shown flashes of potential, the combination of a high-difficulty matchup against McLean and the Zebras' strict 40.0 floor for daily game caps kept him on the bench. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (42.58). He is arguably the most volatile play of the day; his defensive value and speed keep him in the lineup, but the heavy platoon disadvantage against Sale necessitates caution. We are also monitoring the confirmed status of **Casey Schmitt** and **Hyeseong Kim**; should their lineups materialize differently than our projections, we may be forced to pivot, as the margin of error for these marginal starters is razor-thin.",
